WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.280
"NCIS" has stood head and shoulders above&nbsp;
most of its police procedural peers for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.480
thanks to its lovable cast of eclectic characters&nbsp;
and almost uncanny longevity. The CBS show has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.840
been running since 2003, and the ongoing Season&nbsp;
19 finds the series as strong as usual. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.480
it's clear that the show's arguably most massive&nbsp;
change yet is on the not-too-distant horizon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.320
and it's been looking that way for a while.&nbsp;
For 18 years, the stalwart leader of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.680
titular investigation team in "NCIS" has been&nbsp;
Leroy Jethro Gibbs played by Mark Harmon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.880
who was the backbone of the show&nbsp;
throughout its first 18 seasons.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.440
Season 19 of "NCIS" has revealed that new&nbsp;
developments — along with 18 seasons of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.640
hard-hitting investigations weighing&nbsp;
down on his broad shoulders — have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.520
caused Gibbs to decide that&nbsp;
he's done with his NCIS job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.640
and that he's planning to carve a new&nbsp;
life for himself in Alaska. It's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.720
understandable development for the character&nbsp;
for anyone who watched the Season 18 finale.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.360
The episode showed Gibbs boarding a boat that&nbsp;
wasn't destined to last long. As it sailed out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.400
to sea, it unexpectedly blew up. Fortunately,&nbsp;
fans saw Gibbs' body not long afterward with him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:05.200
soon swimming to shore. It let everyone know Gibbs&nbsp;
would return for Season 19, but it definitely gave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.600
the impression he wasn't going to be around much&nbsp;
longer. But what, exactly, caused the character to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.880
decide so — or rather, what prompted Mark Harmon&nbsp;
to join the many actors who have left "NCIS?"

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.440
The Hollywood Reporter states Mark Harmon's exit&nbsp;
from the show is a pretty final one — at least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.600
in his starring capacity. After all, the star&nbsp;
has only signed for a limited amount of episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.400
for Season 19, and Gibbs' decision to remain in&nbsp;
Alaska pretty much removes him from the fabric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.320
of the show for the foreseeable future. What's&nbsp;
more, the ongoing season features some brand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.560
new star power in the form of Katrina Law&nbsp;
and rumored Harmon replacement Gary Cole.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.960
Harmon's limited-episode deal means that Gibbs has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.720
effectively left his active role in the&nbsp;
show behind, but showrunner Steven D.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.080
Binder is quick to note that the actor&nbsp;
will maintain a behind-the-scenes role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.680
and there's always a chance for an&nbsp;
on-screen comeback, as well. Binder stated,

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.280
"As an executive producer and dear friend,&nbsp;
Mark continues to be an integral part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:57.040
the fabric of the show. Our north star has&nbsp;
always been staying true to our characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.680
and that truth has always guided&nbsp;
the stories we tell and where those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.600
characters go. So regarding the future&nbsp;
of Gibbs, as long-time fans of the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.040
may have noticed over the years ...&nbsp;
never count Leroy Jethro Gibbs out."

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.800
That means viewers may not have shed&nbsp;
their last tears over Gibbs just yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.600
If we were into betting, we'd be&nbsp;
willing to put down money on Mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.800
Harmon returning for the series&nbsp;
finale ... whenever that occurs.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.560
It's hard to say goodbye to a beloved TV&nbsp;
character, especially one who's been on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:25.440
air for nearly two decades. Leroy Jethro Gibbs&nbsp;
starred in hundreds of "NCIS" episodes and has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.960
earned a special place in people's hearts.&nbsp;
The show just won't be the same without him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.040
and fans have already taken to social media to let&nbsp;
their thoughts known on the emotional departure.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.800
It's entirely possible his final scene of&nbsp;
fishing on a lake in the great unknown will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.480
be the last time audiences see Gibbs,&nbsp;
but at least he received the send-off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.640
he so richly deserved. Fans were quick to&nbsp;
chime in with their thoughts. One fan wrote,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.680
"I am sad Gibbs [is] leaving&nbsp;
NCIS.. But [got to] respect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.120
and applaud Mark Harmon [for] his&nbsp;
performance thru 18 years as Gibbs."

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.080
Another fan noted,

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.680
"I just learned Mark Harmon is leaving&nbsp;
NCIS and I'm in complete shock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.920
I grew up with NCIS and especially with&nbsp;
agent Leroy Jethro Gibbs but he did his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.720
time and I'm really proud. He&nbsp;
had such an amazing journey."

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.800
Gibbs has certainly come a long way ever since&nbsp;
he first graced people's screens on the episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.960
"Ice Queen" on "JAG." He'd only appear on&nbsp;
one more "JAG" episode before spinning off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.360
into "NCIS," where he's been ever since.&nbsp;
Harmon walked away when the time was right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.200
just like the great Gibbs so famously&nbsp;
said, "When the job is done, walk away."

